.TH GENETREE 1 2000-1月 "discovered_edges" "discovered_edges"
.SH NAME
discovered_edges \- Get the candidate edges that were examined by the residual two-stage structure discovery.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIdiscovered_edges(\fBtree\fR as <generic> XGBoostGRN, 
\fBtop_n\fR as integer = 50, 
\fBaccepted_only\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Get the candidate edges that were examined by the residual two-stage structure discovery.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBtree\fB \fR\- the trained [XGBoostGRN](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GeneTree.XGBoostGRN) model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtop_n\fB \fR\- 
 the number of the records that are ordered by the R² gain in descending order, \fB0\fR
 returns all of them.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBaccepted_only\fB \fR\- when TRUE only the accepted new edges are returned.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a dataframe whose columns are \fBgene\fR, \fBregulator\fR, \fBstatus\fR, \fBcorrelation\fR,
 \fBdelta_r2\fR, \fBr2_before\fR, \fBr2_after\fR, \fBsplits\fR, \fBsensitivity\fR and \fBreason\fR;
 an R# error message object is returned when the model does not contain any discovery
 result.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
the \fBdelta_r2\fR of an accepted edge is the validation R² gain that the edge brought
 to its target gene model, the \fBcorrelation\fR column is the pearson correlation between
 the target gene residual and the candidate gene expression.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
geneTree
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
